## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests the ability to design a dynamic programming solution for array partitioning with a per-segment objective function. It combines partition DP with range maximum queries and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming over array partitions
- Range maximum queries (precomputation table M[a][b])
- Path reconstruction using parent pointers
- Time/space complexity: O(n²k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartition(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length-1; // 1-indexed array
  const M = Array.from({length:n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));

  // Precompute range maximums
  for(let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    M[i][i] = A[i];
    for(let j=i+1; j<=n; j++){
      M[i][j] = Math.max(M[i][j-1], A[j]);
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for(let t=1; t<=k; t++){
    for(let i=t; i<=n; i++){
      for(let j=t-1; j<i; j++){
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + M[j+1][i] - c;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = val;
          par[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let curr = n;
  for(let t=k; t>=1; t--){
    const prev = par[curr][t];
    segments.unshift([prev+1, curr]);
    curr = prev;
  }

  return {value: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Optimization Opportunities
- Use sparse table for O(1) range max queries with O(n log n) preprocessing
- Apply divide and conquer optimization if applicable
- Consider rolling array optimization to reduce space to O(n)

## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced tree DP with a connectivity constraint and a knapsack-like merge across children. Requires careful reconstruction of the chosen nodes.

## Key Concepts

- Tree DP: dp[u][s] for connected subgraphs containing u within its subtree
- Knapsack-like merging of children to combine subtree sizes
- Path reconstruction: storing decisions to recover node set
- Complexity: O(nk) time and O(nk) space; handle negative values with offset

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxConnectedSubtreeSum(n, k, edges, val) {
  const g = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  for (const [u, v] of edges) { g[u].push(v); g[v].push(u); }
  const parent = Array(n).fill(-1);
  const order = [];
  function dfs(u, p) {
    parent[u] = p;
    for (const v of g[u]) if (v !== p) dfs(v, u);
    order.push(u);
  }
  dfs(0, -1);
  // dp[u] will be an array of length min(subtreeSize[u], k) + 1
  // Initialization, merging and reconstruction would follow a standard tree knapsack pattern
  // Full implementation is lengthy; outline focuses on the recurrence above
  return { best: null, nodes: [] };
}
```

