## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with a non-adjacent selection constraint and exact count, forcing clarity on state definition and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP on two dimensions (i, t) with take/skip choices. 
- Non-adjacency enforced by using i-2 when taking i. 
- Backtracking recovers chosen indices; space optimization possible.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKNonAdjacent(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(false));
  for(let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      const val = (i>=2 ? dp[i-2][t-1] : (t===1 ? 0 : -Infinity)) + A[i-1];
      if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = true; }
    }
  }
  let res = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(i>0 && t>0){
    if(take[i][t]){ res.push(i); i-=2; t--; } else { i--; }
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], indices: res};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for at-most k selections? 
- How would you optimize space to O(k)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests 1D partition DP, median-based block costs, and reconstruction; mirrors realistic facility placement.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions
- Median-based block cost
- Prefix sums for O(1) block cost
- Backpointer reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPostOffice(X, k) {
  const n = X.length;
  const cost = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));

  // Precompute prefix sums for O(1) range sum queries
  const prefix = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + X[i];
  }

  // Precompute block costs using median property
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      const m = Math.floor((l + r) / 2);
      cost[l][r] = (X[m] * (m - l) - (prefix[m] - prefix[l])) +
                   ((prefix[r + 1] - prefix[m + 1]) - X[m] * (r - m));
    }
  }

  // DP table and backpointers
  const dp = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let p = 1; p <= k; p++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = p - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const candidate = dp[j][p - 1] + cost[j][i - 1];
        if (candidate < dp[i][p]) {
          dp[i][p] = candidate;
          parent[i][p] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let curr = n;
  for (let p = k; p >= 1; p--) {
    const start = parent[curr][p];
    blocks.unshift([start, curr - 1]);
    curr = start;
  }

  return { cost: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Complexity Analysis
- Time: O(kn²) for DP transitions plus O(n²) for cost preprocessing
- Space: O(nk) for DP table, reducible to O(n) with layer optimization

