## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests clean 0/1 DP layering with an additional teleport operation, requiring careful handling to avoid double-counting and efficient O(mn) time complexity with minimal extra memory overhead.

## Key Concepts
- 0/1 DP layering with an additional operation constraint
- Row/column prefix maxima for efficient teleport transition computation
- Path reconstruction under dual-state DP representation

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSum(grid) {
  const m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
  const dp0 = Array(m).fill().map(() => Array(n).fill(0));
  const dp1 = Array(m).fill().map(() => Array(n).fill(0));

  // Initialize first cell
  dp0[0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp1[0][0] = grid[0][0];

  // Fill DP tables
  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
      if (i === 0 && j === 0) continue;

      // Regular moves without teleport
      dp0[i][j] = Math.max(
        i > 0 ? dp0[i-1][j] : 0,
        j > 0 ? dp0[i][j-1] : 0
      ) + grid[i][j];

      // After teleport or using teleport now
      dp1[i][j] = Math.max(
        i > 0 ? dp1[i-1][j] : 0,
        j > 0 ? dp1[i][j-1] : 0,
        // Teleport from any cell in same row/column
        ...getTeleportOptions(dp0, i, j)
      ) + grid[i][j];
    }
  }

  return Math.max(dp0[m-1][n-1], dp1[m-1][n-1]);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
